Revision history for Authen-WebAuthn
 
0.006
  - Security: decode client-supplied CBOR with CBOR::XS->new_safe, as
    CBOR::XS otherwise calls THAW on any loaded class named by a tag 26
    value (reported by Maurice Aubrey). Requires CBOR::XS 1.84
  - Security: refuse public keys longer than the largest WebAuthn uses
    (600 bytes in COSE, 1100 characters in PEM) before decoding them.
    CryptX takes time quadratic in the size of an RSA key, so one
    registration could take a minute of CPU (reported by Maurice Aubrey)
  - Fix trust_anchors given as a code reference, which was always refused
    (Maurice Aubrey)

0.005
  - Add allow_unknown_attestation_format option

0.004
  - Add allow_untrusted_attestation option

0.003 2023-11-09
  - Update Crypt::OpenSSL::X509::Extension and Net::SSLeay dependancies
  - Make sure Net::SSLeay is initialized before use

0.002 2023-11-09
  - Supported attestation types: none, packed, fido-u2f
  - Mandatory attestation trust chain validation

0.001 2022-01-21
  - initial release
  - Authentication and registration without attestation
  - ECC/RSA keys supported
